(`notes/quadratic_planes.md`). This file is written from the data by `tools/field_lean.py`.

*Lower bound* (`not_colorable_three`). The graph of `data/quadratic_planes/q911.json` has 327 vertices `[a, b, c, e]`,
standing for `((a + b√911)/1560, (c + e√911)/1560)`, and 777 edges. The kernel checks that each edge has length 1
(`checkEdges_E`, `QuadraticPlanes.adj_pt`), and Mathlib's `lrat_proof` checks the LRAT proof
`data/quadratic_planes/q911.lrat` that the colouring formula `q911.cnf` (981 variables, 2660 clauses) is
unsatisfiable. A 3-colouring would satisfy it (`QuadraticPlanes.clause_facts`).

*Upper bound* (`QuadraticPlanes.colorable_four`): `911 ≡ 1² (mod 7)`, so Moorhouse's reduction at 7 applies.
-/

